# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=escort (The Long Haul),
# spec=shaman:elemental, style=dodge, view=844x390,touch, save=carried
# (behaves as fresh per #273 -- playbot's own port is per-run, so
# localStorage never actually carries across separate invocations).
#
# New: direction.md's #7 already has a dodge+escort+shaman:elemental
# reading, but only at 820x1180 portrait (2026-09-25); the only 844x390
# landscape dodge reading on escort used a different spec (warlock:
# destruction, 2026-09-26). Neither of those, nor anything else on #7,
# ever switched styles inside one live match -- every entry is one style
# for the whole pull. This session plays the picked style first to get a
# landscape/shaman datapoint, then switches to `good` partway through the
# same match (no reload, no re-pull) to see whether turning a passive body
# active mid-match can recover lost ground, or whether it only shortens the
# body's own survival the way `good` has on every *other* battleground map
# -- a thing no session has tried yet because every prior comparison was
# two separate pulls, not one pull with a style change inside it.
open
tap battleground
tap map:escort
targets
tap class:shaman:elemental
shot class-picked
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot bg-start
state
ui
play dodge 90
shot mid1
state
bill
wait 2
play dodge 90
shot mid2
state
bill
wait 2
play good 60
shot switched
state
bill
wait 2
play good 60
shot end1
state
bill
says
targets
